== County coding, 1938–77 ==

Florida used numeric county codes on its license plates between 1938 and 1977, with the order of the codes based on the populations of each of the state's 67 counties according to a 1935 census.<ref name="Simpers"/> There was also code 68 on plates ordered from the state tag office in [[Tallahassee, Florida|Tallahassee]], and code 90 on replacement plates.

