==Personalized plates==
Florida offers [[Vanity plate|personalized license plate]]s for an extra fee, on the standard orange blossom design and on specialty designs (below). On the orange blossom design and specialty designs with centered graphics, combinations can consist of between one and seven characters specified by the registrant, including letters, numbers, spaces and hyphens. On specialty designs with left-aligned graphics, combinations are limited to a maximum of five characters, and on the Motorcycle Specialty plate, they are limited to a maximum of six characters.<ref>{{cite web |title=Application for Personalized License Plate |url=https://www.flhsmv.gov/pdf/forms/83043.pdf |publisher=Florida Department of Highway Safety and Motor Vehicles |access-date=February 2, 2021}}</ref>

==Specialty plates==
Florida has offered over 120 specialty license plates to its motorists, most for an extra fee. Some of these plates are no longer issued, while others have been redesigned since they were first issued.<ref name="FLPlateHistory">{{cite web |title=Florida License Plate History |url=https://flhsmv.gov/pdf/about/history/100_years_mv.pdf |publisher=Florida Department of Highway Safety and Motor Vehicles |date=May 2019 |access-date=August 3, 2020}}</ref>

